Audit shutdown coverage
=======================

shutdown_test calls the production workers_shutdown function with injected
monotonic clock, kevent, signal and reap operations. It checks initial and
subsequent clock-read failure, normal grace-period remainder, interrupted
final reaping, descriptor closure and clearing the worker list/count. Real
ordinary descriptors stand in for procdescs; the test does not establish
real protected-worker termination or wall-clock shutdown latency.

session_test uses real channels in the native guest. rate_test covers the
per-session and reconnect-resistant admission limits. policy_test and
submit_test check authenticated identity/event selection and submission rules.
Full bundle activation, actual audit subsystem delivery, protected workers and
SwitchBoard shutdown acknowledgement ordering remain integration gates.

bootstrap_retains_child exercises actual start_session/pdfork with injected
protection denial, then production shutdown reaps the retained child and
closes its descriptor. This replaces the old injected reject_worker test.
failed_watch_retains_worker injects watch failure, checks retained ownership,
then tests successful cleanup and signal/reap errors through shutdown.
Actual protected-worker termination denial and supervisor recovery remain
integration gates; the full main admission loop is not covered by these cases.

lifecycle_test calls the actual daemon main with injected provider, listener,
and event-queue operations. It exercises startup stages, fatal event and accept
errors, successful quiescence and acknowledgement failure. A real stand-in FD
checks queue closure before acknowledgement. Failure paths must destroy any
created provider and must not acknowledge successful quiescence. These cases
use an empty worker list; live protected workers during fatal loop exit remain
a full-system integration gate, alongside the worker-helper coverage above.

shutdown_reports_cleanup_failure injects forced-kill and final-reap errors.
It checks first-error preservation, nonblocking remaining reap attempts, and
release of all tracking nodes and descriptors. Actual denied termination and
supervisor recovery of a surviving protected worker remain integration gates.

exit_event_reap_errors injects an exit event during graceful shutdown and
checks retry after EINTR, propagation of EIO, and acceptance of ECHILD and ESRCH. It
verifies list/count cleanup and actual FD closure without sending SIGKILL to
a child whose exit event was observed. Kernel event delivery and real reap
failure remain separate integration checks.
